It is finally spring in Copenhagen.
I walk over to the window in my living room.
I open it and feel the warm breeze.
The air is fresh and mild this evening.
The evenings are suddenly much lighter now.
The sun is still shining onto my table.
I sit down on my chair.
I take out my travel diary and a blue pen.
I love to write about my experiences in Denmark.
I open to a blank page in the book.
I think about my fantastic weekend.
I was on a long trip yesterday.
I travelled all alone to Odense.
It was my first trip outside Copenhagen.
I smile, because I had a really good day.
Now I want to write it all down.
I put the pen on the paper and begin my story.
